</p>
<pre><code set:text={start} /></pre>
<p>
  The global <code>layr</code> command always runs the version a project has
  installed, so a project never builds with a different LAYR from the one it was
  written for. The <a href="https://layr.dynshift.com/docs">documentation</a> teaches
  the language through live examples that can be edited in place, and every
  snippet in it is compiled in continuous integration.
</p>
